---
// A standalone decision artboard for the wapo case study: why the API's
// atomic unit is the *claim*, not the headline, article, or embedding chunk.
// Four columns show what an agent actually receives for each candidate unit
// (structured but human-readable, not raw JSON) so the failure/win is visible
// rather than argued. Fixed 1600x1200 canvas, #eff3f6 — built to be captured
// as a single figure. Not linked from nav; visit directly.
// Riffs on the "INTERFACE FORM FACTOR EXPLORATION" reference layout.
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#eff3f6" />
    <title>wapo — Choosing the atomic unit</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Why the atomic unit is the claim, not the headline, article, or embedding chunk." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/fish.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="stage">
      <div class="artboard">
        <header class="head">
          <p class="eyebrow">CHOOSING THE ATOMIC UNIT</p>
          <h1>What is the smallest thing this API serves?</h1>
          <p class="principle">
            Principle borrowed from how Context7 chunks docs — the atomic unit is the smallest
            <em>independently-citable</em> thing, and every unit carries its own provenance. Four candidates,
            shown as the agent receives them:
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="cols">
          <!-- 1 — ARTICLE -->
          <section class="col">
            <div class="col-head">
              <span class="cand">Article</span>
              <span class="verdict reject">✗&nbsp; too big</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel">
              <div class="panel-tag mono">one article ⊃ many claims — <span class="warn">no single type · sourcing_tier fits</span></div>
              <div class="blob">
                <p class="blob-line" data-kind="fact">
                  <span class="kind kind-fact mono">reported_fact</span>
                  School closures have spiked 35 percent over the past four years, according to data from the National Center for Education Statistics.
                </p>
                <p class="blob-line" data-kind="quote">
                  <span class="kind kind-quote mono">quote</span>
                  “We call it the big shrink,” said Marguerite Roza, who tracks school funding as director of Georgetown University’s Edunomics Lab.
                </p>
                <p class="blob-line" data-kind="analysis">
                  <span class="kind kind-analysis mono">analysis</span>
                  Experts say the trend will accelerate as relief funds run out.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="note">
              One blob mixes reported fact, analysis, and quotes. To cite anything, the agent has to
              chunk it itself — <strong>re-inheriting the exact problem we're here to solve.</strong>
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 2 — HEADLINE -->
          <section class="col">
            <div class="col-head">
              <span class="cand">Headline</span>
              <span class="verdict reject">✗&nbsp; marketing copy</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel">
              <div class="headline-card">
                <p class="hl-text">Shrinking student populations cause spike in public school closures across U.S.</p>
                <p class="hl-date mono">July 20, 2026</p>
              </div>
              <dl class="fields dim">
                <div><dt class="mono">claim_id</dt><dd class="mono missing">— none</dd></div>
                <div><dt class="mono">sourcing_tier</dt><dd class="mono missing">— none</dd></div>
                <div><dt class="mono">attribution</dt><dd class="mono missing">— none</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </div>
            <p class="note">
              Optimized for human clicks: attribution is compressed out and it goes stale as the story
              develops. <strong>Grounding an agent on headlines is grounding it on marketing copy.</strong>
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 3 — EMBEDDING CHUNK -->
          <section class="col">
            <div class="col-head">
              <span class="cand">Embedding chunk</span>
              <span class="verdict reject">✗&nbsp; drifts</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel">
              <div class="chunk">
                <span class="cut cut-top mono">— chunk boundary · cut by token window —</span>
                <p class="chunk-text">
                  …partly because there are fewer kids in the U.S. Public school closures temporarily
                  slowed during the pandemic as administrators focused on the fallout from covid and tapped
                  relief funds to balance their budgets.
                </p>
                <span class="cut cut-bot mono">— chunk boundary —</span>
                <p class="orphan mono">attribution.speaker <span class="missing">lost — “said Marguerite Roza” landed in the previous chunk</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="note">
              A cosine-similarity window, not a semantic boundary. The quote drifts from its speaker —
              <strong>exactly how attribution breaks in the search tools we'd be replacing.</strong>
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- 4 — CLAIM (selected) -->
          <section class="col selected">
            <div class="col-head">
              <span class="cand">Claim</span>
              <span class="verdict accept">✓&nbsp; selected</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel">
              <div class="claim-id mono"><span class="k">claim_id</span> clm_e5f6</div>
              <p class="statement">“Enrollment at public schools is declining, partly because there are fewer kids in the U.S.”</p>
              <div class="attr-block">
                <span class="env-label mono">attribution</span>
                <dl class="fields tight">
                  <div><dt class="mono">speaker</dt><dd class="mono">Marguerite Roza</dd></div>
                  <div><dt class="mono">setting</dt><dd class="mono">interview</dd></div>
                  <div><dt class="mono">date</dt><dd class="mono">2026-07-18</dd></div>
                </dl>
              </div>
              <dl class="fields">
                <div><dt class="mono">type</dt><dd class="mono">quote</dd></div>
                <div><dt class="mono">sourcing_tier</dt><dd class="mono">on_record</dd></div>
                <div><dt class="mono">content_type</dt><dd class="mono">reporting</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="envelope">
                <span class="env-label mono">article · provenance, rides along not content</span>
                <div class="env-row mono"><span class="k">title</span> Shrinking student populations cause spike in public school closures</div>
                <div class="env-row mono"><span class="k">url</span> wapo.st/3xY2z</div>
                <div class="env-row mono"><span class="k">published</span> 2026-07-20</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="note">
              An attributed statement + sourcing metadata in an article-provenance envelope. Drop any single
              claim into context and <strong>it still knows where it came from.</strong> The <code>claim_id</code>
              is the handle <code>verify</code> and correction-tracking hang off later.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <footer class="foot">
          <p class="mono">
            THE REMAINING RISK IS UPSTREAM OF THE SCHEMA: CLAIMS ONLY STAY CLEAN IF THE
            EDITORIAL PIPELINE MINTS THEM CONSISTENTLY — A NEWSROOM-TOOLING PROBLEM THIS CONCEPT DOESN'T SOLVE.
          </p>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --board-bg: #eff3f6;
    --panel-bg: #ffffff;
    --panel-line: #32404f1f;
    --reject: #b0553f;
    --accept: #2f7d63;
    --wapo-blue: #6b8afd;
  }

  body {
    background: #e2e7ec;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 40px;
  }

  /* Fixed capture canvas. */
  .stage {
    width: 1600px;
    height: 1200px;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }
  .artboard {
    width: 1600px;
    height: 1200px;
    background: var(--board-bg);
    padding: 64px 72px 56px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* ---- header ---- */
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .principle {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 980px;
  }
  .principle em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* ---- columns ---- */
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .col-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .cand {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 27px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .verdict {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .verdict.reject { color: var(--reject); }
  .verdict.accept { color: var(--accept); }

  /* ---- panel shared ---- */
  .panel {
    height: 600px;
    background: var(--panel-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 22px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #32404f0d, 0 8px 24px -16px #32404f30;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .col.selected .panel {
    border: 2px solid var(--wapo-blue);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #32404f0d, 0 12px 32px -14px #6b8afd55;
  }

  .note {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 18px;
    min-height: 84px;
  }
  .note strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .note code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    background: #32404f0f;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .missing { color: var(--faint); }
  .warn { color: var(--reject); }

  /* ---- 1 · article blob ---- */
  .panel-tag {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--faint);
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--panel-line);
  }
  .blob { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
  .blob-line {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.42;
    color: var(--fg);
    padding-left: 12px;
    border-left: 3px solid;
  }
  .blob-line[data-kind='fact'] { border-color: #6b8afd; }
  .blob-line[data-kind='quote'] { border-color: #d98a3d; }
  .blob-line[data-kind='analysis'] { border-color: #9b7fce; }
  .kind {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    margin-right: 8px;
    vertical-align: 2px;
  }
  .kind-fact { background: #6b8afd1f; color: #4a63c9; }
  .kind-quote { background: #d98a3d24; color: #a8641f; }
  .kind-analysis { background: #9b7fce22; color: #6f52a3; }

  /* ---- 2 · headline ---- */
  .headline-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .hl-text {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .hl-date {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }
  .fields { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .fields.dim { opacity: 0.92; }
  .fields > div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--panel-line);
    padding-bottom: 11px;
  }
  .fields > div:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .fields dt { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--faint); }
  .fields dd { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg); text-align: right; }

  /* ---- 3 · chunk ---- */
  .chunk { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }
  .cut {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--reject);
    opacity: 0.75;
    padding: 4px 0;
  }
  .chunk-text {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--fg);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--reject);
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--reject);
    padding: 14px 0;
    margin: 4px 0;
  }
  .orphan {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-top: 18px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* ---- 4 · claim ---- */
  .claim-id {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--faint);
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-line);
  }
  .claim-id .k, .env-row .k { color: var(--wapo-blue); margin-right: 8px; }
  .statement {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .attr-block {
    padding-left: 14px;
    border-left: 2px solid #6b8afd55;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .attr-block .env-label {
    color: #4a63c9;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .col.selected .fields > div { padding-bottom: 8px; }
  .fields.tight > div { padding-bottom: 6px; }
  .col.selected .fields { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .envelope {
    background: #6b8afd0f;
    border: 1px solid #6b8afd33;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 13px 14px;
  }
  .env-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #4a63c9;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }
  .env-row {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--fg);
    line-height: 1.5;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .env-row + .env-row { margin-top: 6px; }

  /* ---- footer ---- */
  .foot {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--panel-line);
  }
  .foot p {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--faint);
    max-width: 1100px;
  }
</style>
